<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, to obtain a tree decomposition of <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, we set <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(t)\coloneqq\beta^{\prime}(t)\cup X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(t)\coloneqq\beta^{\prime}(t)\cup X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in V(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in V(T)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The resulting tree decomposition <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> is now a tree decomposition of <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with independence number at most</p>
